SUMMARY:Seattle Film Society In Focus: Tyler Michael James (2022)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T212000
DTSTAMP:20261016T020000Z
UID:seattle-film-society-in-focus-tyler-michael-james-2026-10-15-19:00:00-
 07:00
DESCRIPTION:LOW LIFE follows Benny\, a small-time YouTube star who catches
  predators online\, experiences a night from hell when he lets one of them
  into his own home.\n\nLOW LIFE will be preceded by a screening of the fil
 m’s proof-of-concept short\, and a conversation about James’s film & c
 areer will follow the screening. This event is presented in partnership wi
 th the Northwest Film Forum.\n\nThursday October 15th at the Northwest Fil
 m Forum. Doors at 6:30\, Film at 7. See you at the movies!\n\nThe Seattle 
 Film Society’s IN FOCUS showcase series returns this October with a scre
 ening of Tyler Michael James’s 2022 thriller LOW LIFE!\n\nhttps://nwfilm
 forum.org/films/seattle-film-society-in-focus-tyler-michael-james/\n\nEsti
 mated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Staff Selects - The Daytrippers (1996)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T192000
DTSTAMP:20261024T003000Z
UID:staff-selects-the-daytrippers-2026-10-23-17:30:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:With its droll humor and bittersweet emotional heft\, the feat
 ure debut of writer-director Greg Mottola announced the arrival of an unas
 sumingly sharp-witted new talent on the 1990s indie film scene. When she d
 iscovers a love letter written to her husband (Stanley Tucci) by an unknow
 n paramour\, the distraught Eliza (Hope Davis) turns to her tight-knit Lon
 g Island family for advice. Soon the entire clan—strong-willed mom (Anne
  Meara)\, taciturn dad (Pat McNamara)\, and jaded sister (Parker Posey) wi
 th pretentious boyfriend (Liev Schreiber) in tow—has squeezed into a sta
 tion wagon and headed into Manhattan to find out the truth\, kicking off a
  one-crazy-day odyssey full of unexpected detours and life-changing revela
 tions. Performed with deadpan virtuosity by a top-flight ensemble cast\, T
 he Daytrippers is a wry and piercing look at family bonds stretched to the
  breaking point.\n\nScreening as a part of our quarterly Staff Selects ser
 ies! This film was chosen and presented by Camille Hermida-Fuentes\, our D
 irector of Operations! \n\nGreg Mottola\, 1996\, Canada\, 87 min\, in Engl
 ish\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/staff-selects-the-daytrippers/\n\nEst
 imated start: 17:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
