BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TRAUMA BOND: A Serbian Film (2026 Extended Cut) (2010)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T220500
DTSTAMP:20261024T030000Z
UID:trauma-bond-a-serbian-film-2026-extended-cut-2026-10-23-20:00:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:This Halloween series is co-presented by Monday Mourning and S
 carecrow Video\, where every ticket directly benefits the world’s larges
 t physical media archive\, so no romance\, no comedy\, not even New French
  Extremity\, is lost to time. Each Trauma Bond screening features a live D
 rag pre-show with Miss Monday.\n\nAn aging porn star agrees to participate
  in an “art film” in order to make a clean break from the business\, o
 nly to discover that he has been drafted into making one of the harshest f
 ilms ever made. In order to escape his living cinematic hell and save his 
 family’s life\, Milos will have to sacrifice everything – his pride\, 
 his morality\, his sanity\, and maybe even his own life.\n\nSrđan Spasoje
 vić\, 2010\, Serbia\, 104 min\, in Serbian with English Subtitles\n\nhttp
 s://nwfilmforum.org/films/trauma-bond-a-serbian-film-2026-extended-cut/\n
 \nEstimated start: 20:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TRAUMA BOND: Come and See (1985)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T224500
DTSTAMP:20261010T030000Z
UID:trauma-bond-come-and-see-2026-10-09-20:00:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:This Halloween series is co-presented by Monday Mourning and S
 carecrow Video\, where every ticket directly benefits the world’s larges
 t physical media archive\, so no romance\, no comedy\, not even New French
  Extremity\, is lost to time. Each Trauma Bond screening features a live D
 rag pre-show with Miss Monday.\n\nThis widely acclaimed film from Soviet d
 irector Elem Klimov is a stunning\, senses-shattering plunge into the dehu
 manizing horrors of war. As Nazi forces encroach on his small village in p
 resent-day Belarus\, teenage Flyora (Aleksei Kravchenko\, in one of the sc
 reen’s most searing depictions of anguish since Renée Falconetti’s Jo
 an of Arc) eagerly joins the Soviet resistance. Rather than the adventure 
 and glory he envisioned\, what he finds is a waking nightmare of unimagina
 ble carnage and cruelty—rendered with a feverish\, otherworldly intensit
 y by Klimov’s subjective camerawork and expressionistic sound design. Ne
 arly suppressed by Soviet censors who took eight years to approve its scri
 pt\, Come and See is perhaps the most visceral\, impossible-to-forget anti
 war film ever made.\n\nElem Klimov\, 1985\, Soviet Union\, 142 min\, in Ru
 ssian and German with English Subtitles\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/t
 rauma-bond-come-and-see/\n\nEstimated start: 20:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TRAUMA BOND: Irreversible (2002)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T215500
DTSTAMP:20261017T030000Z
UID:trauma-bond-irreversible-2026-10-16-20:00:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:This Halloween series is co-presented by Monday Mourning and S
 carecrow Video\, where every ticket directly benefits the world’s larges
 t physical media archive\, so no romance\, no comedy\, not even New French
  Extremity\, is lost to time. Each Trauma Bond screening features a live D
 rag pre-show with Miss Monday.\n\nOne night. An unforgivable act. A tale t
 old in reverse.\n\nAcclaimed filmmaker Gaspar Noé’s unflinching explora
 tion of human savagery and the uncompromising nature of time\, Irreversibl
 e was met with a groundswell of acclaim and uproar upon its premiere at Ca
 nnes in 2002. Stylish\, sexually frank\, and brutal\, the film’s conceit
  of exploring the events of one terrible night on the streets of Paris in 
 reverse chronological order was celebrated and derided in equal measure\, 
 helping to further cement Noé’s legacy as a cinematic enfant terrible.
 \n\nGaspar Noé\, 2002\, France\, 93 min\, in English\, French\, Italian\,
  and German with English Subtitles\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/trauma
 -bond-irreversible/\n\nEstimated start: 20:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:True Stories (1986)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261007T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261007T212000
DTSTAMP:20261008T023000Z
UID:true-stories-2026-10-07-19:30:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:There is perhaps no film to come out of the Reagan era that is
  as optimistic and positive about American life than David Byrne’s True 
 Stories.\n\nInspired by absurd tabloid clippings he collected while on tou
 r with Talking Heads with the question of “what if this was all true\,
 ” Byrne managed to create a collage of average middle-American life that
  elevates its subjects to the extraordinary. Moving between computer chip 
 plants\, mall fashion shows\, and basement Voodou rituals\, True Stories b
 ecomes the inverse of a film like David Lynch’s Blue Velvet (released th
 e same year!) in that it seeks to find the good hidden underneath the (som
 etimes) hard exterior of American life deep in the heart of Texas.\n\nDavi
 d Byrne\, United States\, 1986\, 89 min\, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforu
 m.org/films/true-stories/\n\nEstimated start: 19:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:True Stories (1986)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T205000
DTSTAMP:20261009T020000Z
UID:true-stories-2026-10-08-19:00:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:There is perhaps no film to come out of the Reagan era that is
  as optimistic and positive about American life than David Byrne’s True 
 Stories.\n\nInspired by absurd tabloid clippings he collected while on tou
 r with Talking Heads with the question of “what if this was all true\,
 ” Byrne managed to create a collage of average middle-American life that
  elevates its subjects to the extraordinary. Moving between computer chip 
 plants\, mall fashion shows\, and basement Voodou rituals\, True Stories b
 ecomes the inverse of a film like David Lynch’s Blue Velvet (released th
 e same year!) in that it seeks to find the good hidden underneath the (som
 etimes) hard exterior of American life deep in the heart of Texas.\n\nDavi
 d Byrne\, United States\, 1986\, 89 min\, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforu
 m.org/films/true-stories/\n\nEstimated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Truth To Fiction: Cameraperson (2016)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T213500
DTSTAMP:20261106T033000Z
UID:truth-to-fiction-cameraperson-2026-11-05-19:30:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:A boxing match in Brooklyn\; life in postwar Bosnia and Herzeg
 ovina\; the daily routine of a Nigerian midwife\; an intimate family momen
 t at home: these scenes and others are woven into Cameraperson\, a tapestr
 y of footage captured over the twenty-five-year career of documentary cine
 matographer Kirsten Johnson. Through a series of episodic juxtapositions\,
  Johnson explores the relationships between image makers and their subject
 s\, the tension between the objectivity and intervention of the camera\, a
 nd the complex interaction of unfiltered reality and crafted narrative. A 
 work that combines documentary\, autobiography\, and ethical inquiry\, Cam
 eraperson is both a moving glimpse into one filmmaker’s personal journey
  and a thoughtful examination of what it means to train a camera on the wo
 rld.\n\nKirsten Johnson\, United States\, 2016\, 102 min\, in English\, Bo
 snian\, Farsi\, Hausa\, and Arabic with English subtitles\n\nhttps://nwfi
 lmforum.org/films/truth-to-fiction-cameraperson/\n\nEstimated start: 19:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WTF with STUFF - Holy Trinity (2019)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T205500
DTSTAMP:20261022T020000Z
UID:wtf-with-stuff-holy-trinity-2026-10-21-19:00:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:After an incident huffing her drug of choice—a mysterious ae
 rosol can from the ubiquitous Glamhag brand—Trinity finds herself with a
  newfound gift for speaking to the dead. Confused and more than a little c
 urious about this strange turn of events\, she seeks the counsel of a colo
 rful cast of characters\, from priests and drag queens to a witch and more
 \, all of whom teach her their unique spiritual practices.\n\nAs she navig
 ates life with this unexpected talent (and continues to huff that mysterio
 us drug)\, Trinity is tossed between hallucination and reality more and mo
 re frequently\, developing a growing confidence in her strange new ability
  and learning to harness it in surprising ways. But with any great power c
 omes great responsibility\, and soon Trinity has to decide what’s more i
 mportant: her community and personal relationships or the allure of influe
 nce and fame\n\nBoasting an inclusive cast (including Theo Germaine from N
 etflix’s The Politician) and crew comprised of diverse communities often
  neglected in mainstream cinema and approaching typically taboo subjects w
 ith verve and acceptance\, Holy Trinity is a sometimes raunchy\, always en
 tertaining celebration of all that makes us different. In their feature fi
 lm debut\, writer\, director and star Glamhag presents a vibrant and vivid
  portrait of friendship\, spirituality and community\, with more than a li
 ttle glam sprinkled in along the way.\n\nGlamhag\, 2019\, United States\, 
 91 min\, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/wtf-with-stuff-holy-t
 rinity/\n\nEstimated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Who Moves America
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T205000
DTSTAMP:20261020T020000Z
UID:who-moves-america-2026-10-19-19:00:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:As the world’s largest package delivery company\, UPS moves 
 millions of packages across more than 200 countries and territories each d
 ay – and its workforce holds the power to bring that machine to a halt. 
 Who Moves America follows a UPS driver in California casting his first str
 ike vote\, a Teamster in New York who walked the picket line during the hi
 storic 1997 strike\, and a warehouse worker in Kentucky balancing night sh
 ifts with community college\, weighing whether she can afford to say no\, 
 as well as access to the General President of the International Brotherhoo
 d of Teamsters\, Sean O’Brien. As they and their co-workers organize\, a
 rgue\, and campaign across the country\, the film builds toward a single\,
  high-stakes vote: accept the deal\, or risk everything for a strike that 
 could reshape the American economy. Through intimate access and on-the-gro
 und storytelling\, Who Moves America reveals the human stories behind the 
 single largest collective bargaining agreement in North America and explor
 es the power and complexity of collective action in modern America.\n\nYae
 l Bridge\, United States\, 2026\, 87 min\, in English\, German\, Italian\,
  and French with English subtitles\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/who-mo
 ves-america/\n\nEstimated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
